<newsitem itemid="50788" id="root" date="1996-09-12" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Oriel H1 pre-tax profits higher, holds div.</title>
<headline>Oriel H1 pre-tax profits higher, holds div.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (pence) continuing  ops			   5.84		   vs 3.33</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 19.81		  vs 0.68</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  2.0		    vs 2.0</p>
<p> Turnover		    13.13		  vs 11.57</p>
<p> Pretax			6.67		   vs 1.08</p>
<p>Profit on sale of  discontinued ops	  5.16		   vs nil</p>
<p> Operating profit	  2.01		   vs 1.35</p>
<p> Interest payable	  0.50		   vs 0.27</p>
<p> Tax			   0.66		   vs 0.70</p>
<p> Net taxed		   6.01		   vs 0.38</p>
<p> Attributable		5.75		   vs 0.19</p>
<p> Retained profit	   5.17		   vs 0.37 loss</p>
<p> Pay date		    December 2</p>
<p> Div registration date   November 12</p>
<p>NOTE - Insurance broker Oriel Group Plc said it expects to see good progress over the next 18 months.</p>
<p>&quot;While the group is expanding, I do not feel that it is appropriate to increase the dividend as cash can be better deployed elsewhere,&quot; chairman Nigel Cayzer said in a statement.</p>
<p>Cayzer said Oriel continues to recieve approaches regarding possible offers for the group.</p>
<p>&quot;The board will want to ensure any offer fully reflects the confidence they have in the prospects of the business based on foundations built over the last two years,&quot; Cayzer added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
